{"id":"CVE-2018-20852","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-07-13T20:29:42.000Z","updated":"2026-10-07T18:24:46.612Z","description":"http.cookiejar.DefaultPolicy.domain_return_ok in Lib/http/cookiejar.py in Python before 3.7.3 does not correctly validate the domain: it can be tricked into sending existing cookies to the wrong server. An attacker may abuse this flaw by using a server with a hostname that has another valid hostname as a suffix (e.g., pythonicexample.com to steal cookies for example.com). When a program uses http.cookiejar.DefaultPolicy and tries to do an HTTP connection to an attacker-controlled server, existing cookies can be leaked to the attacker. This affects 2.x through 2.7.16, 3.x before 3.4.10, 3.5.x before 3.5.7, 3.6.x before 3.6.9, and 3.7.x before 3.7.3.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-20 CWE-20 Improper Input Validation"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":4.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugs.python.org/issue35121","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://python-security.readthedocs.io/vuln/cookie-domain-check.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2019/08/msg00022.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20190817 [SECURITY] [DLA 1889-1] python3.4 security update"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-08/msg00071.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1988"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-08/msg00074.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1989"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2019/08/msg00040.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsou