{"id":"CVE-2018-1000030","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-02-08T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:03:21.344Z","description":"Python 2.7.14 is vulnerable to a Heap-Buffer-Overflow as well as a Heap-Use-After-Free. Python versions prior to 2.7.14 may also be vulnerable and it appears that Python 2.7.17 and prior may also be vulnerable however this has not been confirmed. The vulnerability lies when multiply threads are handling large amounts of data. In both cases there is essentially a race condition that occurs. For the Heap-Buffer-Overflow, Thread 2 is creating the size for a buffer, but Thread1 is already writing to the buffer without knowing how much to write. So when a large amount of data is being processed, it is very easy to cause memory corruption using a Heap-Buffer-Overflow. As for the Use-After-Free, Thread3->Malloc->Thread1->Free's->Thread2-Re-uses-Free'd Memory. The PSRT has stated that this is not a security vulnerability due to the fact that the attacker must be able to run code, however in some situations, such as function as a service, this vulnerability can potentially be used by an attacker to violate a trust boundary, as such the DWF feels this issue deserves a CVE.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":3.6,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oyR9DAZjZK_SCn3mor6NRAYLJS6ueXaY/view","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3817-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3817-2"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201811-02","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201811-02"},{"url":"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/sj3ee7xv55j36k7/AADwP-YfOYikBMuy32e0uvPFa?dl=0","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3817-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3817-1"},{"url":"https://bugs.python.org/issue31530","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujan2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["python"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1000117","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-03-07T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T01:37:10.621Z","description":"Python Software Foundation CPython version From 3.2 until 3.6.4 on Windows contains a Buffer Overflow vulnerability in os.symlink() function on Windows that can result in Arbitrary code execution, likely escalation of privilege. This attack appears to be exploitable via a python script that creates a symlink with an attacker controlled name or location. This vulnerability appears to have been fixed in 3.7.0 and 3.6.5.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/5989","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://bugs.python.org/issue33001","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["microsoft","python"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1000802","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-09-18T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:03:31.390Z","description":"Python Software Foundation Python (CPython) version 2.7 contains a CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection') vulnerability in shutil module (make_archive function) that can result in Denial of service, Information gain via injection of arbitrary files on the system or entire drive. This attack appear to be exploitable via Passage of unfiltered user input to the function. This vulnerability appears to have been fixed in after commit add531a1e55b0a739b0f42582f1c9747e5649ace.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4306","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-4306"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/09/msg00031.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180926 [SECURITY] [DLA 1520-1] python3.4 security update"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3817-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"USN-3817-2"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/8985/commits/add531a1e55b0a739b0f42582f1c9747e5649ace"},{"url":"https://mega.nz/#%21JUFiCC4R%21mq-jQ8ySFwIhX6WMDujaZuNBfttDVt7DETlfOIQE1ig"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/8985"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3817-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"USN-3817-1"},{"url":"https://bugs.python.org/issue34540"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/09/msg00030.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180925 [SECURITY] [DLA 1519-1] python2.7 security update"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2020-01/msg00040.html","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2020:0086"},{"url":"https://